<title>USA: Security Capital Pacific Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Security Capital Pacific Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>EL PASO, Texas 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.28		    $0.27</p>
<p> FFO shr		     0.38		     0.35</p>
<p> Net			 26,141		   25,771</p>
<p> Revs			84,555		   73,577</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  75,147		   72,211</p>
<p>		 YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.46		    $0.93</p>
<p> FFO shr		     1.44		     1.30</p>
<p> Net			130,711		   84,319</p>
<p> Revs		     326,246		  264,873</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  73,057		   67,052</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The full name of the company is Security Capital Pacific Trust.</p>
<p>FFO (funds from operations) per share reflects pro forma data assuming the spin-off of PTR's Homestead Village extended-stay lodging assets as of January 1, 1995.</p>
<p>All figures except FFO do not give effect to spin-off of Homestead assets. FFO excluding the effect of the Homestead spin-off for Q4 total $0.39 a share in 1996 and $0.38 in 1995.</p>
<p>Year FFO not giving effect to spin-off of Homestead assets $1.57 vs $1.45.</p>
</text>
